#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567135} :activity/id #uuid "b6e9d445-0ba2-5cbc-973a-1de35aa7f2c5" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048206 :topic/id #uuid "8850e3a0-f2fb-5671-843a-13422a22aa79" :topic/math-academy-id 4387} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567118 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567019 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "200ed653-8d22-5eba-808d-7a37690a4d53" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/81/8108b38989765e84ab83817d82352bf1d18249a0c7c5d19bc940480564f91d5d.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566432} {:answer/id #uuid "21d1343b-7100-58e3-bed7-c7d90bf7a16a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/17/17aa625cfbc90322745b214bca0c4857885d4338e3628e25074668c832cf0732.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566435} {:answer/id #uuid "46294241-6d76-5660-8308-b704b82c7087" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/d8/d823dd4dcd675b07b004cf2850059600e861c8b3d259f884d25c61e43431de35.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566501} {:answer/id #uuid "579c7f1d-d6a9-5e5b-bcc9-c804ba1b38f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/93/93cc14e996746f6516b412eeb4c71f8df7439bf7d210e36a6b67412feec08225.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566528} {:answer/id #uuid "d37321c7-1ae7-5d15-94e2-6426d7989dee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/78/78347152f7962f733ea97e43a799f3f1c8318a4ac18608125d26dbd318f664bd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566779}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186566501} :answer-field/id #uuid "02a5f76b-f604-59fe-97b6-05e2a5373e9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566877}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "151c9aa4-1f7d-5ae4-bc54-fb829989618a" :question/math-academy-id "q-184529" :question/problem "Let $I=[0,1]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=[i,1]\\times \\{i\\}.$ Which of the following represents ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the union of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *at least one* set:\n\n$$\n{⋃}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for at least one}\\,\\,k\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{0.5}=[0.5,1]\\times \\{0.5\\}=\\{(k,0.5)\\,:\\,k\\in [0.5,1]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a horizontal line segment from the point $(0.5,0.5)$ to the point $(1,0.5)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/bb/bb8f515fb5c342ece5727830e95bcc617c03a5bf6542f959ba9e020d22f7faef.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[i,1]\\times \\{i\\}=\\{(k,i)\\,:\\,k\\in [i,1]\\}\n$$\n\nis the horizontal line segment from the point $(i,i)$ to the point $(1,i).$ \n\n![](images/f2/f255d7dede080e93cb135c1087a0f14591467439d891187062a4fa185a8858cf.png)\n\nAs $i$ runs over $I,$ these line segments sweep the following triangle that represents the union ${⋃}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}:$\n\n![](images/d8/d823dd4dcd675b07b004cf2850059600e861c8b3d259f884d25c61e43431de35.png)"} :step/id #uuid "25a9e4f2-d080-581c-9f8c-5e235244e694"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567123 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567095 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01577e1c-b63e-57f0-b602-f5ed9e7c099b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/8e/8e2511ab8e06ba3d994e4a5ad13c53867d47265d1407a3a4995ee477a83eb471.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566363} {:answer/id #uuid "0f84b057-93cf-5d03-ad21-48cde768543f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/89/89ac9e71d8152097657f0c01daecf2b894dc142db4ba27fbfadcb8ded6e9cb19.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566393} {:answer/id #uuid "1fc3fdb8-5fd0-510e-90c2-ef266178bfdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/d3/d3b71b596aef1bc509c1501c0b8020890f0801a37a61116a8733593a7d2780d4.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566429} {:answer/id #uuid "23d1723d-bafd-5e2d-8f64-068977702f1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/4a/4aee0f1bf6bfc1f54a5255fdadd9049bfb44f712d34ee61491bec32d1cb6b42e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566438} {:answer/id #uuid "38371641-9dae-5512-8405-cadb1d0e3763" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/20/2086bcf65608ff2c031da9f6882272fd6d8eb828f3d904c4f0fc946b5fbe108c.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566478}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186566478} :answer-field/id #uuid "279053a0-a4df-5eac-9836-abf0190a8617" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566894}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e159fb00-748b-54e2-99d5-3850d85771a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-181780" :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S={R}^{+}\\times Z$ in the Cartesian plane?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS={R}^{+}\\times Z\n$$\n\n \ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is a positive real number and whose $y$-coordinate is an integer number.\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in {R}^{+},\\,y\\in Z\\}\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S,$ consider ${S}_{-1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any positive real number and whose $y$-coordinate equals $-1.$\n\n$$\n{S}_{-1}=\\{(x,-1)\\,:\\,x\\in {R}^{+}\\}\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{-1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/50/50228bcff5b3678518379cda03257ac234e8312cd23f9b38fa897188c8c5c1c5.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any positive real number and whose $y$-coordinate equals $1.$\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}=\\{(x,1)\\,:\\,x\\in {R}^{+}\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/75/75f8be8dd49241503b705c78e4018a98fead197191b38f856d7fbce069a63de2.png)\n\nWe can create the subsets $…,{S}_{-3},{S}_{-2},{S}_{0},{S}_{2},{S}_{3},…$ similarly. Our Cartesian product consists of the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{+}\\times Z & =…{S}_{-2}\\cup {S}_{-1}\\cup {S}_{0}\\cup {S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\\cup {S}_{3}\\cup … \\\\  & ={⋃}_{i\\in Z}{S}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize ${R}^{+}\\times Z$ as the set of horizontal lines shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/20/2086bcf65608ff2c031da9f6882272fd6d8eb828f3d904c4f0fc946b5fbe108c.png)"} :step/id #uuid "40115689-6ef7-5297-b4cc-659f1af4234d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567136}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567135 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198717 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70258a9c-ad3c-5850-8748-1f4a0d3a1177" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/df/df4a1ecffe6302ee57250944ec8f178f46a066b2edff2ed1afb200e7b0217cf7.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282651} {:answer/id #uuid "8e44c058-ebf0-58a9-b42c-cf19c1b27b1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/6b/6b5b39546eabacdf948bd87e793727fdc8cd8f2664df037be53bfb630fc41670.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282922} {:answer/id #uuid "9b97d722-59cf-5bfa-b1e2-78edadab4a20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/17/17a176a0e7cb254483d93741cd2c1e3db581005f479928ac36809e55bc970c07.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283047} {:answer/id #uuid "e63db0fe-0384-58ea-87bc-2b3a3a552ef0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$∅,$ the empty set" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283695} {:answer/id #uuid "f5247f03-9735-58c9-b61d-6fb0019f18b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/50/506d86848903de9f038d541152aabf67d99d0f4d0a7e5f5772b811ff1cf9dade.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283835}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186283695} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9980425-ccef-5f6c-bf0f-d1c5beef9b70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284314}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "30b7b0c8-79fe-53ad-bb30-601d2f7e078d" :question/math-academy-id "q-172690" :question/problem "Let $I=[0,2]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=\\{i\\}\\times [0,i].$ Which of the following represents ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the intersection of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *all* the sets:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for all}\\,\\,k\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=1,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}=\\{1\\}\\times [0,1]=\\{(1,k)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,1]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a vertical line segment from the point $(1,0)$ to the point $(1,1)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](images/71/71dd97607df48caf579c2e476520507ede035f65c336064f022cd900b6c120fc.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\{i\\}\\times [0,i]=\\{(i,k)\\,:\\,k\\in [0,i]\\}\n$$\n\nis the vertical line segment from the point $(i,0)$ to the point $(i,i).$ \n\n![](images/4b/4b87c830620f54e5b3a3bb7923be971b4d9d4abb98cfb3dcdc8387f376a0b452.png)\n\nThere are no points that lie in all sets. Therefore, the intersection of the indexed sets is $∅,$ the empty set."} :step/id #uuid "8b7cd465-a531-5b2c-aa31-225a1dbba8b6" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567123}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567136 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287775 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d39a817-0adb-550e-8e47-c0b77a693527" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/68/687ed490e4b4bf72689bc2da100a5ec01d4d853fbf9d1a5297cb288e40774d1e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285050} {:answer/id #uuid "2cbee043-5ba2-528d-8aee-063f374c9411" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/e4/e4298479aa0cdbbdb394b08e921fb42c4de25deab1f08874d0de0144bbad9053.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285182} {:answer/id #uuid "390fc2d2-01dd-5e3c-a297-12c139db3beb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/76/761e56f14b968a8485c5acf6c648fe04448d374d0f2375f0b5e473953262e958.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285322} {:answer/id #uuid "5986320c-c7fe-52ac-83d2-f4c986dd6a15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/34/34770ca1c57cf00c5779a435dbbc72bf74e024433d8210ce0ea912a22f51008a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285606} {:answer/id #uuid "8ab43c53-7822-528e-ada6-d161755d6289" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/a1/a1a9065f9dbb6648100bc6a22bff367916c241dc2eba5f3878d6cf1b9821d4e8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286059}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286059} :answer-field/id #uuid "4cb2ecd2-7336-5c6e-953e-301306a51187" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287316}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "dd0c147c-869f-5ac6-b075-b382d08ceaa2" :question/math-academy-id "q-181960" :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=[0,2]\\times \\{-1,0,1\\}$ in the Cartesian plane?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS=[0,2]\\times \\{-1,0,1\\}\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,2]$ and whose $y$-coordinate is either $-1,0,$ or $1.$\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in [0,2],\\,y\\in \\{-1,0,1\\}\\}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,2]$ and whose $y$-coordinate equals $-1$\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}=\\{(x,-1)\\,:\\,x\\in [0,2]\\}\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/de/de9bd6dc79cabf8230b0cec26233958aa0fbb001875b9942cbb7f4d36e6b08fb.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{2}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,2]$ and whose $y$-coordinate equals $0.$\n\n$$\n{S}_{2}=\\{(x,0)\\,:\\,x\\in [0,2]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/81/819c31e4d29dbd3e18c7dea8df495a565d2ede866ec019c764704d6dc47f5c70.png)\n\nNow, consider ${S}_{3}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate is any real number in the interval $[0,2]$ and whose $y$-coordinate equals $1.$\n\n$$\n{S}_{3}=\\{(x,1)\\,:\\,x\\in [0,2]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis set is represented by the line segment shown below.\n\n![](images/3f/3f335df98dc9cb33ccc96f87d24efa3bd78a4d4c271d0fbaf7ae5e8c30916d9e.png)\n\nOur Cartesian product is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\nS={S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\\cup {S}_{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $S$ can be represented by the three line segments shown below.\n\n![](images/a1/a1a9065f9dbb6648100bc6a22bff367916c241dc2eba5f3878d6cf1b9821d4e8.png)"} :step/id #uuid "929b7ead-827c-5b82-82c3-38ca98ce721d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567138}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567138 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567008 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dbee5dc-e5a6-52c6-8ec3-191a184237ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/25/25c6e0dbdeeec44456e198ed668cf23be3f64f97ecdbf8ab172412d689066bba.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566390} {:answer/id #uuid "9ec3fbfa-8578-50e3-ae33-5ae3fa1b23ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/25/25bd7ebe8087af06fa21e4d5f9878d0e5867630372138bad1af241c1ee270d30.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566670} {:answer/id #uuid "c0815e68-d37c-5b08-9b24-7ed04211e59e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/2d/2df87b90d770a5f2c0ba40a55330409d1cd80866b7e34299eab6dcbf675c6a13.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566743} {:answer/id #uuid "cf2c4ec1-bc76-5b71-8506-5c91d013652b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/80/80c13426f812f1e98b0ffd61d81eeb7c70a04c5013625d6e6d2add5f2d4a6d85.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566772} {:answer/id #uuid "d3d84521-ef3e-5c0c-b7b9-6d3a3526d965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497} :answer/value "images/32/32c33c9eb7df58d8550a00a1318f6d56e0755916ffeedafd71e13d93431e4911.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566780}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186566670} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3874236-333b-5468-b929-21203a72fc65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566956}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "025f0441-54cd-515d-9989-fed405f3f4cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-181972" :question/problem "Which of the following is a representation of the set $S=Z\\times {Z}_{0}^{-}$ in the Cartesian plane?" :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian product $A\\times B$ consists of all ordered pairs whose first coordinate belongs to $A$ and whose second coordinate belongs to $B.$\n\n$$\nA\\times B=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in A,\\,b\\in B\\}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the set \n\n$$\nS=Z\\times {Z}_{0}^{-}\n$$\n\ncontains every point in ${R}^{2}$ whose $x$-coordinate is an integer number and whose $y$-coordinate is a negative integer or zero..\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,x\\in Z,\\,y\\in {Z}_{0}^{-}\\}.\n$$\n\nTo visualize $S$, consider ${S}_{-1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $-1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is negative integer or zero.\n\n$$\n{S}_{-1}=\\{(-1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in {Z}_{0}^{-}\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{-1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/a5/a5d50bdd40efb18b4d29f3e108576e3befcc0d3f3e5b54a0686aeef6e9ffa212.png)\n\nNext, consider ${S}_{1}⊂S$ containing all points whose $x$-coordinate equals $1$ and whose $y$-coordinate is any negative integer or zero.\n\n$$\n{S}_{1}=\\{(1,y)\\,:\\,y\\in {Z}_{0}^{-}\\}.\n$$\n\nWe can represent ${S}_{1}$ in the plane as follows:\n\n![](images/12/129cb0ae2a59415a90118030461244ab7f1faa91aba47b5e0e2864323dbfede9.png)\n\nWe can create the subsets $…,{S}_{-3},{S}_{-2},{S}_{0},{S}_{2},{S}_{3},…$ similarly. Our Cartesian product $S$ is the *union* of these subsets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}S & =…\\cup {S}_{-3}\\cup {S}_{-2}\\cup {S}_{-1}\\cup {S}_{0}\\cup {S}_{1}\\cup {S}_{2}\\cup {S}_{3}\\cup … \\\\  & ={⋃}_{i\\in Z}{S}_{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can visualize $Z\\times {Z}_{0}^{-}$ as the set of points in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/25/25bd7ebe8087af06fa21e4d5f9878d0e5867630372138bad1af241c1ee270d30.png)"} :step/id #uuid "9b20313e-470b-5bfd-bcdb-18795605d3de" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567118}}] :activity/title "Visualizing Cartesian Products" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186566357}]}
